
# Cloud Document Access Requirements

## 1. Supported Cloud Storage Providers
- Support Google Drive.
- Support Microsoft OneDrive.
- Allow users to connect either or both providers.

## 2. Connect Account
- Provide a "Connect Google Drive" option.
- Provide a "Connect OneDrive" option.
- Authenticate using the respective provider's OAuth 2.0 flow.
- Require explicit user consent before accessing files.
- Only connect cloud storage to the currently logged-in website account.

## 3. Document Access
- Allow users to browse documents in their connected cloud storage.
- Allow users to select documents from Google Drive or OneDrive.
- Display document name, file type, and relevant metadata.
- Allow users to search for documents.
- Allow users to access or import selected documents into the website.
- Support commonly used document types (PDF, DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, TXT, etc.).

## 4. Permissions & Privacy
- Request the minimum permissions required.
- Prefer read-only access unless document editing is explicitly required.
- Do not access files without user consent.
- Do not expose cloud storage credentials or access tokens to the frontend.
- Store OAuth tokens securely.
- Only access files authorized by the user.
- Do not scan or access unrelated files without explicit user action.

## 5. Account Management
- Allow users to disconnect Google Drive.
- Allow users to disconnect OneDrive.
- Handle expired tokens and re-authentication gracefully.
- Handle revoked permissions gracefully.
- Allow users to reconnect their accounts.

## 6. User Experience
- Show connection status for each provider.
- Display clear authorization and error messages.
- Provide loading indicators while retrieving documents.
- Allow users to retry failed document retrieval.
- Clearly identify the source of each document (Google Drive or OneDrive).

## 7. Security
- Use OAuth 2.0 securely.
- Validate authentication and authorization on the backend.
- Encrypt tokens at rest.
- Use secure session management.
- Avoid logging access tokens or sensitive document content.
- Ensure users cannot access another user's connected accounts or documents.

## 8. Acceptance Criteria
- Users can connect Google Drive.
- Users can connect OneDrive.
- Users can browse and select documents from either provider.
- Users can access selected documents through the website.
- Access is restricted to the permissions granted by the user.
- Users can disconnect their cloud accounts at any time.
- Token expiration and revoked access are handled securely.
